\f0\fs36 \cf0 A PLACE TO REMEMBER (badge: Memory) \'97 PENDING WORK, plain-language list\
Last updated: 2026-08-25 (#18-new \'97 the outsider's report has now been\
checked, and most of what it flagged turns out to be things we decided\
on purpose. It had no way of knowing that. The code is in better shape\
than the report made it sound, so the answer to "mend or rebuild" is\
mend.\
Three real holes were left. My Week's cure was started and its first\
step is built and tested: a chore's checkmark now clears wherever the\
app runs instead of only when you open My Week. Nothing has gone onto\
the phone.\
Bare session numbers below mean the old shared chain.)\
\
This is the "what's still left" list in everyday words. Nothing here\
is urgent. Finished work isn't tracked here \'97 git history keeps the\
full record \'97 so this list stays short.\
\
\
WHAT'S NEXT\
------------------------------------------------------------------\
- THE REMINDERS \'97 OPEN AGAIN (#14-new, #15-new, #16-new). Reading\
  the whole of the reminder machinery found eight faults. Two are\
  fixed and the third \'97 the big one, the fault you reported \'97 is\
  fixed on one screen of three.\
  The fault: a thing you tick off early still reminds you, because\
  those three screens use the phone's own repeating alarm and a\
  repeating alarm fires whether or not the item is done. The cure is\
  to give each one a single moment aimed at the next time it is due,\
  worked out fresh every time the app runs, so it can skip one you\
  have already done. You agreed to that on one condition \'97 that a\
  missed firing is noted when you open the app \'97 and that part is\
  already built.\
  What #16-new put in:\
    Pets is cured. A feed you have already logged does not call out\
      again that day, and still calls out the next day.\
    Each feed is set two days ahead rather than repeating forever.\
      Two was your call. The trade is real and worth knowing: if the\
      app goes unopened longer than that, nothing new gets set and\
      the reminder simply does not arrive. The pop-up tells you\
      afterwards; it cannot make it arrive.\
    Your places on the phone: the app can hold 56 reminders. At two\
      days ahead, your fourteen items will use 28 of them, so there\
      is room to spare. The Scheduled Reminders screen tells you how\
      full it is, so you never have to take my word for the number.\
    One test that had never been run since the very beginning now\
      runs on the Mac: a day passing, an item ticked off, and\
      whether it still reminds tomorrow.\
    Two small things you may notice when this reaches the phone: a\
      feed shows up twice on the Scheduled Reminders screen instead\
      of once, because two days are set; and it says it does not\
      repeat, which is now true.\
  What #17-new put in:\
    My Day is cured, the same way Pets was. A thing you have already\
      logged does not call out again that day, and still calls out\
      the next day.\
    The day-counting the two screens share now lives in one place\
      instead of being written out twice.\
  What #17-new found out, and this is the part that matters:\
    My Week has the fault too. Its reminder never looks at the\
      checkmark at all, so a chore you have ticked still sounds on\
      its day. Our own notes have been saying the opposite \'97 that My\
      Week was the one screen that never had this problem \'97 and\
      there is even a test in place holding the wrong behaviour\
      still. The note and the code were allowed to disagree and\
      nothing caught it.\
    The tests that pass do not test the thing you care about. They\
      check the pieces on their own. Nothing checks the whole chain \'97\
      you tick something, and the reminder does not sound. That has\
      never been tested, which is the plainest explanation yet for\
      why eight sessions of work still left faults.\
    There may be more. The outsider only had one look, and most of\
      what it reported has not been double-checked yet. What is\
      confirmed and what is not is marked item by item in\
      docs/outside-review.md.\
  What #18-new checked, and this is the good news:\
    Most of what the outsider flagged is not broken. It read the code\
      with none of our notes in front of it, so it could not know\
      which things were decided on purpose. Six of them were: a Done\
      button not silencing the repeat, the To-Do banner carrying only\
      OK, Orders no longer raising reminders, two occurrences ahead,\
      the snooze being written on the item, and the pop-up that\
      speaks when a list cannot be read. All six still hold.\
    So it is mend, not rebuild. The joins are careful and reasoned,\
      not loose. What is left is a short list of specific holes.\
    The three real holes: My Week ignoring the checkmark; Siri\
      marking something done without telling the reminder module;\
      and a failed daily clear-out not stopping the run.\
    One new one, in no record before: when Siri marks an item done,\
      nothing re-works the reminders. It sends you to My Day, and My\
      Day clears the day but does not rebuild anything. Siri also\
      leaves a snooze in place.\
    Confirmed about the tests: there is no test at all for the\
      module's top, for any screen, or for the housing. Ten test\
      files, all of them the pieces on their own.\
  What #18-new put in \'97 My Week, step one of three:\
    A chore's checkmark now clears wherever the app runs, instead of\
      only when you open My Week. That arithmetic used to live on\
      the page; it now lives with the rest of the reminder work and\
      has twenty tests of its own.\
    Why that had to come first: My Week's reminder is the phone's\
      repeating kind, which returns forever. If the app simply\
      skipped a ticked chore, the repeat would be cancelled and only\
      come back when the checkmark cleared \'97 and the checkmark only\
      cleared when you opened the page. A chore ticked once would\
      have gone silent for good. Worse than the fault we started\
      with.\
    Steps two and three, still to do: teach the day-counting to\
      count in weeks, then rewrite My Week's reminder to use it and\
      to look at the checkmark. The wrong note and the wrong test\
      that say My Week never had the fault go out with step three.\
  Also found and left alone (#18-new, your call): the warning about\
  a failed clear-out is never actually shown to you. It is written\
  down but filtered out before it reaches the pop-up, because it was\
  classed as harmless. It is not harmless \'97 a failed clear-out can\
  cancel a reminder for something you never did.\
  What #15-new put in:\
    A pop-up when you open the app, if something went wrong. Until\
      now the app could fail at reminders completely and look\
      perfectly well. It speaks about the four things that mean a\
      reminder will not arrive, and stays quiet about the two that\
      do not. It comes back once a day rather than every time you\
      come back to the app, so it does not become something you\
      tap away without reading.\
    A note of what never reached you, in the same pop-up. Written\
      down as the day rolls over, since that is the last moment the\
      app can still see what was left undone. One line per item,\
      the most recent, in your Still To Do wording. Shown once and\
      gone when you tap it. Being away a fortnight gives you a\
      short list, not a wall.\
  Still to do, in order: My Week steps two and three; Siri telling\
  the module what it has done; making a failed clear-out speak;\
  holding a run that gets dropped when two happen at once; saying\
  the show-a-banner instruction once instead of on eight pages;\
  bringing My Week's snooze under the module; and the dead "+1 Day"\
  button.\
  The plan that ran the earlier work is no longer\
  a live file; it is kept whole at the end of docs/build-history.md\
  in case anyone ever needs to know why a thing was done its way.\
  What was built, step by step:\
    Step 1 (#6-new) \'97 the new piece itself, plus its tests. No\
      page touched.\
    Step 2 (#7-new) \'97 My Day and Pets stopped arming their own.\
      This is the fix for the silence.\
    Step 3 (#8-new) \'97 My Week, Look Ahead and To-Do stopped too,\
      and Orders came out of the reminding altogether.\
    Step 4 \'97 the snoozes, delays and postpones, in three pieces:\
      My Week's postpone and Look Ahead's delay (#9-new), then My\
      Day's and Pets' snoozes (#10-new), and then To-Do (#11-new),\
      which needed nothing built. A To-Do banner has never had a\
      Snooze button to tap, so the piece was taking out code that\
      could never run.\
    Step 5 (#11-new) \'97 the Memory Test's five-minute recall.\
    Step 6 (#11-new) \'97 the warning when your phone can't hold\
      every reminder asked for. It shows as you save the item,\
      on the page you're on, and says the reminder furthest in\
      the future won't go off until something makes room.\
    Step 7 (#11-new) \'97 the clean slate. Yesterday's checkmarks,\
      snoozes and counts now clear whether or not you open My Day\
      or Pets, and any banner from before today is taken down as\
      the app opens or comes back to the front. A Done always\
      means today now.\
    Step 8 (#12-new) \'97 Scheduled Reminders, in Settings under the\
      three reminder times. It shows every reminder your phone is\
      holding, under Today, Tomorrow, This Week and Later, with\
      the soonest first. Tap any one and you get the whole story\
      of it: what it is, which page it came from, when it fires\
      and whether it repeats, when it was last due and when it's\
      next due, exactly what the banner will say, and which\
      buttons it will carry. At the foot it tells you how full\
      the phone is. Timer alerts are counted there but not\
      listed, your call \'97 the Timer is for short stretches and\
      isn't something you'd look up.\
      It cannot tell you whether a reminder actually went off.\
      The phone keeps no record of that once a banner is\
      dismissed, so there is nothing to read. What it does\
      instead is show you when each one was DUE \'97 so if a\
      repeating reminder is missing from the list, that's the\
      problem; if it's sitting there properly set and you heard\
      nothing, the app did its part.\
  You built all of this, put it on the phone, and it was all\
  readable. What still hasn't happened is the morning after.\
- The clock setter is off by twelve hours (#5-new). Spinning the\
  hour down from the 12:00 PM it opens at goes to 11 PM instead\
  of 11 AM, so setting 9 in the morning the natural way lands on\
  9 at night \'97 which is your evening banner. Typing the time is\
  fine, and so is the AM/PM button. Small fix on its own. After\
  it, any time you set by spinning needs checking.\
- Look Ahead: change the tile format, and change or drop the\
  Snooze (#3-new).\
- Timer: add a Stop (Pause) / Continue (Go) button to the tile,\
  and add a log (#3-new).\
- Vault restructuring: the "Home" header button becomes a "Back"\
  button (#3-new).\
- Scheduled Reminders, two layout fixes (#15-new): the header sits\
  too low on the screen, and the total number of reminders should\
  be noticeable directly under the header.\
